# mulga-eks-provider-id and mulga-vpc-mtu are role-agnostic: every EKS node,
# server or agent, needs the kubelet drop-in and the flannel VXLAN MTU pin
# regardless of which role the first-boot selector picks. So unlike the
# role-selected units in eks-server's 40- file, these are unconditional here.
#
# This has to be a preset file rather than the postinst's `systemctl enable`:
# mkosi runs preset-all after every profile's postinst, resetting every unit to
# policy and discarding whatever the postinst asked for. With no policy file at
# all the fallthrough is "enable" anyway, so this changes nothing about the
# image shipped today — but that "today" only holds because nothing
# contradicts the default, and stating it here means an upstream package
# change can't silently flip it.
#
# Numbered ahead of eks-server's 40- and eks-agent's 50- so a future rename
# collision would be caught by first-match-wins favouring the more specific
# file, not this common one; today the unit sets don't overlap at all.
enable mulga-eks-provider-id.service
enable mulga-vpc-mtu.service
